{"id":2,"date":"2025-09-01T21:14:40","date_gmt":"2025-09-01T21:14:40","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/?page_id=2"},"modified":"2025-09-06T04:01:27","modified_gmt":"2025-09-06T04:01:27","slug":"home-v2","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/","title":{"rendered":"Stop T.H.E.M."},"content":{"rendered":"\n<style>\n  @font-face {\n    font-family: 'Akzidenz-Grotesk Next';\n    src: url('https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/AkzidGrtskNext-Black.woff2') format('woff2');\n    font-weight: 900;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-display: swap;\n  }\n\n  @font-face {\n    font-family: 'Helvetica';\n    src: url('https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/helveticaneue-bold.woff2') format('woff2');\n    font-weight: 900;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-display: swap;\n  }\n\n  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing:border-box; margin:0; padding:0; }\n\n  .fancy-container {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 1rem;\n    max-width: 1200px;    \n    margin: 2rem auto;\n    padding: 0 1rem;\n  }\n\n  .container-title {\n    flex: 1;\n    padding: 1.5rem;\n    text-align:center;\n    font-family: 'Akzidenz-Grotesk Next';\n    font-size: 16pt;\n  }\n\n  .container-body {\n    flex: 2;\n    padding: 1.5rem;\n    text-align:left;\n  }\n\n  .container-body > p {\n    width: 85% !important;\n    font-family 'Helvetica';\n    font-size: 12pt;\n  }\n  .container-body > ol {\n    width: 85% !important;\n    font-family 'Helvetica';\n    font-size: 12pt;\n  }\n\n  .container-body-left {\n    border-left: 1px solid #000000;\n  }\n  .container-body-right {\n    border-right: 1px solid #000000;\n  }\n\n  .asset-wrapper {\n    max-width: 1200px;\n    margin: auto;\n    display: flex;\n  }\n  .asset-wrapper-right {\n    justify-content: flex-end;\n  }\n  .asset-wrapper-left {\n    justify-content: flex-start;\n  }\n\n  .asset-wrapper img {\n    display: block;\n    width: 150px;\n    height: auto;\n  }\n\n  @media (max-width:600px) {\n    .asset-wrapper { display:none; }\n    .fancy-container { padding: 0; }\n    .fancy-container-left { flex-direction: column; }    \n    .fancy-container-right { flex-direction: column-reverse; }\n    .container-title { padding: 0; width: 95% !important; }\n    .container-body { padding: 0; width: 95% !important; }\n    .container-body-left { border-left: none; }\n    .container-body-right { border-right: none; }\n  }\n<\/style>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"fancy-container fancy-container-left\">\n  <div class=\"container-title container-title-left\">\n    <h1>WE CAN WIN<\/h1>\n  <\/div>\n\n  <div class=\"container-body container-body-left\">\n    <p>The fight against Energy Fuels\u2019 attempts to transport, haul, extract, and mill uranium stretches back many decades. From the early 1980s onward, resistance to what\u2018s now called the \u201cPinyon Plain Mine\u201d just south of the Grand Canyon was aided by a bearish uranium market. This meant Energy Fuels was unable to profitably extract uranium from the mine. This changed after the company secured a contract with the Department of Energy, the manufacturer of the United States\u2019 nuclear weapons. Each new generation of the nuclear age must rise to defend water, the sacred, the Earth, and life itself. From the mines across the west to the White Mesa Mill in Utah, onward to Honeywell\u2019s Metropolis Works in IL, the secretive weapons plants beyond, or their headquarters in Lakewood CO: everywhere there are opportunities to break this cycle.<\/p>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"asset-wrapper asset-wrapper-right\">\n  <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/asset-2.png\" alt=\"\">\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"fancy-container fancy-container-right\">\n  <div class=\"container-body container-body-right\">\n    <p>Since the Navajo Nation&#8217;s government sold out the people to enter into a partnership with Energy Fuels, allowing for uranium transport through the Navajo Nation, elders across Havasupai and Dine territories have asked: <em>when will the people rise up to stop them?<\/em> All legislative and legal avenues have been exhausted! After four decades of struggle to protect the people and the land from the destructive forces of the uranium industry&mdash;including the designation of a new monument and dozens of lawsuits by indigenous nations and environmental groups&mdash;it is clear that our moment requires a new, direct intervention.<\/p>\n    <ol>\n      <li>Take any and all necessary actions against Energy Fuels&#8217; transport, hauling, extraction, and milling. There are many points of intervention. <em>Choose your own adventure<\/em>.<\/li>\n      <li>Send your contributions to <a href=\"mailto:stopthemsubmissions@protonmail.com\">stopthemsubmissions@protonmail.com<\/a>. For example, you could send information on coming events, or report-backs from actions taken. You could send designs for graphics like posters or memes.<\/li>\n      <li>Spread the word.<\/li>\n      <li>Get organized! Here&#8217;s how to form an <a href=\"https:\/\/crimethinc.com\/zines\/how-to-form-an-affinity-group\">affinity group<\/a>.<\/li>\n    <\/ol>\n  <\/div>\n  <div class=\"container-title container-title-right\">\n    <h1>TAKE ACTION<\/h1>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"asset-wrapper asset-wrapper-left\">\n  <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/asset-2.png\" alt=\"\">\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"fancy-container fancy-container-left\">\n  <div class=\"container-title container-title-left\">\n    <h1>YOUR ENEMY<\/h1>\n  <\/div>\n\n  <div class=\"container-body container-body-left\">\n    <dl>\n    <dt>Energy Fuels<\/dt>\n    <dd>URL: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.energyfuels.com\">www.energyfuels.com<\/a><\/dd>\n    <dd>Address: 225 Union Blvd, Suite 600, Lakewood CO 80228<\/dd>\n    <dt>Pinyon Plain Mine Location<\/dt>\n    <dd><a href=\"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/pinyon-plain-mine.jpeg\">Pinyon Plain Mine Map<\/a><\/dd>\n    <dd>Traveling north along highway 64 towards the Grand Canyon, turn right on Forest Road 305.  Follow this road directly to the mine.  You can confirm you&#8217;re on the right track by following: \n      <ul style=\"width: 90%;\">\n        <li>the best maintained road within the web of dirt roads the intersect the route<\/li> \n        <li>the electrical lines along FR305 from the small substation near the intersection with HWY 64 all the way to the mine<\/li>\n        <li>the frequent placards along FR 305 indicating it is a uranium hauling route.<\/li>\n      <\/ul>\n    <\/dd>\n    <dd>GPS coordinates: 35.882953002251, -112.09469908531773<\/dd>\n    <dt>Haul Route &#038; Times<\/dt>\n    <dd><a href=\"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/haul-route.jpeg\">Haul Route Map<\/a><\/dd>\n    <dd>Times: 8:30 AM &#8211; 3 PM, weekdays<\/dd>\n    <dt>Mill Location<\/dt>\n    <dd>6425 S US-191, Blanding, UT 84511, USA<\/dd>\n    <dt>Hammon Trucking Information<\/dt>\n    <dd>URL: <a href=\"https:\/\/hammontrucking.com\">https:\/\/hammontrucking.com<\/a><\/dd>\n    <dd>Address: 940 N Box Elder Street, Hildale UT 84784-0837<\/dd>\n    <\/dl>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"asset-wrapper asset-wrapper-right\">\n  <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/asset-2.png\" alt=\"\">\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"fancy-container fancy-container-right\">\n  <div class=\"container-body container-body-right\">    \n    <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/ef-global-projects.jpeg\">A global map of Energy Fuels projects<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.grandcanyontrust.org\/act\/i-oppose-uranium-mining-near-grand-canyon\/\">Grand Canyon Uranium Mining Petition<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.biologicaldiversity.org\/programs\/public_lands\/mining\/Grand_Canyon_Uranium_Mining\/index.html\">Grand Canyon Uranium Mining Overview from the Center for Biological Diversity<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/protectwhitemesa.org\">Protect White Mesa<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/haulno.com\">Haul No<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.dine-care.org\">Dine Care<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/linktr.ee\/TheMathues\">The Matheus<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.sierraclub.org\/arizona\">Sierra Club Grand Canyon Chapter<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.antiuraniummappingproject.com\">Anti-Uranium Mapping Project<\/a><\/li>\n    <\/ul>\n  <\/div>\n\n  <div class=\"container-title container-title-right\">\n    <h1>RESOURCES<\/h1>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"asset-wrapper asset-wrapper-left\">\n  <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/asset-1.png\" alt=\"\">\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>WE CAN WIN The fight against Energy Fuels\u2019 attempts to transport, haul, extract, and mill uranium stretches back many decades. From the early 1980s onward, resistance to what\u2018s now called the \u201cPinyon Plain Mine\u201d just south of the Grand Canyon was aided by a bearish uranium market. This meant Energy Fuels was unable to profitably [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-2","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/2","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/stopthem.global\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https: